        "char_end": 313,
        "char_start": 0,
        "effective_step": 1,
        "end_token_index": 84,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 85,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Identify the given angles and their relationships.\n- Angle \\(BAD\\) is trisected into three equal parts, each measuring \\(x\\).\n- Angle \\(CDA\\) is also trisected into three equal parts, each measuring \\(y\\).\n- The external angles at \\(B\\) and \\(D\\) are given as \\(110^\\circ\\) and \\(100^\\circ\\) respectively."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 627,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 629,
        "char_start": 315,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 197,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 198,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Calculate the internal angles at \\(B\\) and \\(D\\).\n- Since the external angle at \\(B\\) is \\(110^\\circ\\), the internal angle at \\(B\\) is \\(180^\\circ - 110^\\circ = 70^\\circ\\).\n- Similarly, since the external angle at \\(D\\) is \\(100^\\circ\\), the internal angle at \\(D\\) is \\(180^\\circ - 100^\\circ = 80^\\circ\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 846,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 848,
        "char_start": 631,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 270,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 271,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Express the internal angles at \\(B\\) and \\(D\\) in terms of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\).\n- The internal angle at \\(B\\) can be expressed as \\(2x + x = 3x\\).\n- The internal angle at \\(D\\) can be expressed as \\(2y + y = 3y\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1048,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1050,
        "char_start": 850,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 353,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 354,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Set up equations based on the internal angles.\n- From Step 2, we know \\(3x = 70^\\circ\\), so \\(x = \\frac{70}{3}^\\circ\\).\n- From Step 2, we know \\(3y = 80^\\circ\\), so \\(y = \\frac{80}{3}^\\circ\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1456,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1458,
        "char_start": 1052,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 469,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 470,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Determine the measure of angle \\(AFD\\).\n- Angle \\(AFD\\) is formed by the intersection of the trisectors of angles \\(BAD\\) and \\(CDA\\).\n- Since \\(AFD\\) is an exterior angle to triangle \\(AEF\\) and considering the symmetry and properties of the trisectors, angle \\(AFD\\) is the sum of the non-adjacent internal angles of the trisectors at \\(A\\) and \\(D\\), which simplifies to \\(180^\\circ - (x + y)\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1674,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1676,
        "char_start": 1460,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 567,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 568,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Calculate the value of angle \\(AFD\\).\n- Substitute the values of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\): \\(AFD = 180^\\circ - \\left(\\frac{70}{3} + \\frac{80}{3}\\right) = 180^\\circ - \\frac{150}{3} = 180^\\circ - 50^\\circ = 130^\\circ\\)."
      }
    ]
